invariant: INV-16
file: chacha20.c
catches: test/chacha-builds.sh
reason: chacha20.c guards chacha20_xor's call to the vector path on a macro no
  build defines, so a host object's chacha20_xor runs the portable loop.
  Nothing else objects: chacha20_vector.c still compiles and links,
  bin/chacha20_equiv_test calls it directly, and every vector passes,
  because the portable loop computes the same bytes; only the time is
  wrong. Every session of a host object runs the vector ChaCha20, so the
  script compiles chacha20.c as a host object does and requires
  chacha20_xor's own body to call chacha20_vector_xor.

